      },
      "text": "Soil is a three-phase system — solid (minerals + organic matter), liquid (soil water + dissolved nutrients), and gas (air) — inhabited by a community of organisms. Horticultural practice is fundamentally about managing these phases to optimize plant growth."
    },
    {
