        "title": "Soil Science for Horticulture",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "LIQUID PHASE (~25% of volume when at field capacity):\n    Soil water contains dissolved ions: NO₃⁻, H₂PO₄⁻, K⁺, Ca²⁺, Mg²⁺, etc.\n    Water potential gradient drives movement root → plant."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-SOIL-SCIENCE.md#007",
      "path": [
        "04-SOIL-SCIENCE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
