        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Soil Science for Horticulture",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "GAS PHASE (~25% of volume when at field capacity):\n    N₂, O₂, CO₂ (higher than atmosphere), water vapor.\n    O₂ availability critical for root respiration and microbial activity.\n    Waterlogged soil: gas phase eliminated → anaerobic stress.\n```"
