        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Soil Science for Horticulture",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nPARTICLE SIZE COMPARISON:\n  Sand: visible to naked eye (0.05–2mm). Like small ball bearings.\n        High drainage; low surface area; low nutrient holding.\n  Silt: not visible (0.002–0.05mm). Smooth, flour-like when dry.\n        Moderate properties; crusts easily.\n  Clay: microscopic platelets (<0.002mm). Flat, sheet-like.\n        ENORMOUS surface area: 1g of clay = 5–800 m² surface area.\n        This surface area is why clay holds water and nutrients."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-SOIL-SCIENCE.md#017",
      "path": [
        "04-SOIL-SCIENCE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
