        "section": "horticulture",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Soil Science for Horticulture",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "CLAY MINERALS (two main types in temperate soils):\n  Kaolinite: 1:1 structure (1 silica: 1 alumina layer).\n             Low CEC, low shrink-swell. Dominant in tropical weathered soils.\n  Smectite (Montmorillonite): 2:1 structure.\n             High CEC, high shrink-swell. Dominant in many temperate soils.\n             This is why black clay soils crack in summer and swell in winter.\n```"
    },
