        "title": "Soil Science for Horticulture",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "IMPLICATIONS FOR MANAGEMENT:\n  Tillage: breaks up compaction but destroys aggregates.\n           No-till: aggregates develop over time; but compaction risk.\n  Organic matter additions: cements aggregates; improves stability.\n  Foot traffic / machinery: compacts macro pore space.\n  Wetting/drying cycles: can help or harm structure depending on clay type.\n```"
